# Bento glass cards (canonical UI)

For service/vertical/feature tiles, **always** reuse the bento glass card pattern from `services-section` — not flat strips, plain bordered boxes, or generic Material cards.

Reference: `exprimer-web/src/app/sections/services-section/`

## Structure

```html
<div class="bento">
  <div class="bento__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <a class="bento-card bento-card--{accent}" [routerLink]="...">
    <span class="bento-card__rim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="bento-card__top">
      <span class="bento-pill">Status</span>
      <span class="bento-card__index">01</span>
    </div>
    <!-- optional visual / meters / session / checks -->
    <div class="bento-card__body">
      <h3>Title</h3>
      <p>Summary</p>
      <span class="bento-btn">CTA</span> <!-- or .bento-cta -->
    </div>
  </a>
</div>
```

## Visual rules

- Glass: dark translucent fill + `backdrop-filter: blur`, thin light border, ~24–28px radius
- Rim glow via `.bento-card__rim` + accent CSS vars (`--accent`, `--accent-2`, `--glow`)
- Soft nebula backdrop only behind the grid (`.bento__glow`) — not full-page purple wash
- Accent map: `media` (violet/pink), `talent` (gold/rose), `trust` (emerald/amber)
- Micro-UI inside cards: pills, meters/progress, avatars, check rows — keep one purpose per card
- CTA: gradient pill `.bento-btn` with matching glow, or text `.bento-cta`
- Type: site fonts (`--font-display` / `--font-body`); titles compact, muted body `#b8b8c8`

## Layout

- Asymmetric bento grid (e.g. one tall span-2 + two stacked); collapse to single column ≤900px
- Cards are **links/buttons** (interactive) — justified card chrome only when tappable
- Hover lift + stronger glow; always have tap target ≥44px on coarse pointer
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Do / don’t

```scss
// ✅
.bento-card {
  --accent: #c084fc;
  --accent-2: #f472b6;
  --glow: rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.45);
  border-radius: 28px;
  background: linear-gradient(165deg, rgba(255,255,255,.07), rgba(255,255,255,.02) 42%), rgba(12,12,16,.72);
  backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
}

// ❌ full-bleed image strips, gray Material cards, purple-on-white marketing blocks,
//    hover-only reveal with no click route, empty decorative cards
```

When adding new verticals or similar modules, extend this pattern (new accent token + micro-UI) instead of inventing a new card system.

`/media` uses home2-style **collections** cards (`collections-section`) with the same glass/rim/glow language.

## Forms & selects

- Enquiry/contact forms use the same glass card chrome (`cta-section`).
- Native `<select>` is not allowed for branded UI — use modular `app-glass-select` (`shared/glass-select`) with `ControlValueAccessor`, backdrop on touch, flip-above placement, and Escape/outside click close.

## Brand & WhatsApp

- Header brand mark: `/brand/exprimer-logo.png` (not plain text).
- Floating WhatsApp uses modular `app-whatsapp-fab` (`shared/whatsapp-fab`) — pass `phone` (default `7011982275`); do not hardcode ad-hoc FAB markup elsewhere.
- Back-to-top uses modular `app-scroll-top` (`shared/scroll-top`) — sits above WhatsApp on the right; do not hardcode duplicate scroll buttons.
- Social icons use modular `app-social-links` (`shared/social-links`) — LinkedIn `https://www.linkedin.com/company/exprimer-group/`, Instagram `https://www.instagram.com/exprimergroup/`; Facebook only if URL provided.
